vu0: the R register. VRNEXT stepped a made-up generator and never wrote its
destination register, so every VU0 random number KH2 asks for (403 VRNEXTs,
mostly in effect code: particle sizes, spreads, lifetimes) was whatever ft
held before. Now R is the VU's 23-bit LFSR in the mantissa of a float in
[1, 2): VRNEXT steps it (PCSX2's feedback) and writes ft's dest fields, VRGET
reads it, VRINIT/VRXOR load and mix only the low 23 bits.

